  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/parosphromenus-linkei-1",
      "html": "<p>Parosphromenus filamentosus, the spiketail licorice gourami, belongs to the Parosphromenus genus (licorice gouramis). IUCN Red List: Endangered (very high risk of extinction in the wild). It is one of the larger licorice gouramis and is named for the filament on the male's tail. The Parosphromenus Project calls it one of the least specialized species in the genus and a good choice for less experienced keepers, though like all paros it needs live food.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25a-perchlike-fishes-1-labyrinth-fishes/parosphromenus_cf_filamentosus_ampah_en/",
      "html": "<p>A pretty new species of licorice gourami. It is very close to P. filamentosus and grows to around 3 cm long.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/parosphromenus-linkei-1",
      "html": "<p>Described in 1981 from southeastern Borneo, where it lives in jungle river systems near Banjarmasin.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25a-perchlike-fishes-1-labyrinth-fishes/parosphromenus_cf_filamentosus_ampah_en/",
      "html": "<p>This species originates from Borneo (southeast Kalimantan), where it can be found between Ampah and Muarateweh.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "habitat",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/parosphromenus-linkei-1",
      "html": "<p>Peat swamp forest and blackwater streams near Banjarmasin, an area where much of the forest has been cleared.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "aquariumSize",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/parosphromenus-linkei-1",
      "html": "<p>Keep a pair in 20 litres, or a group of 3 to 6 in 40 litres, with plenty of caves and leaf litter.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "maintenance",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25a-perchlike-fishes-1-labyrinth-fishes/parosphromenus_cf_filamentosus_ampah_en/",
      "html": "<p>Like all licorice gouramis, the species prefers small, single-species tanks, soft and acidic water and fine live food.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "waterConditions",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/parosphromenus-linkei-1",
      "html": "<ul><li>TDS: 0 to 50</li><li>pH: 4.0 to 6.0</li><li>Temperature: 22 to 28°C</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/parosphromenus-linkei-1",
      "html": "<p>Micropredator. They only eat live food. Live baby brine shrimp, daphnia and blackworms are fed.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/parosphromenus-linkei-1",
      "html": "<p>Peaceful and shy. They can share a tank with tiny, calm blackwater fish such as Boraras. Never mix different Parosphromenus species.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "dimorphism",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25a-perchlike-fishes-1-labyrinth-fishes/parosphromenus_cf_filamentosus_ampah_en/",
      "html": "<p>Females can be recognized easily by the completely transparent caudal fin.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "dimorphism",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/parosphromenus-linkei-1",
      "html": "<p>The male's pointed caudal fin ends in a filament and has a brown-red center, a broad black frame and a thin white to blue edge. The dorsal and anal fins repeat this pattern in brown-red or blue-green. Pelvic fins are green-blue with long filaments. The body is bronze, and courting males can turn very dark overall. Females are pale, with a pointed tail and only a faint filament.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/parosphromenus-linkei-1",
      "html": "<p>Cave spawner with a head-down courtship. The male builds probably the most distinct foam nest in the genus, carrying air down from the surface several times. Clutches are usually 50 to 70 eggs and can reach about 200. No special conditions are needed beyond standard licorice gourami care.</p>"
    }
  ],
